duties:
Major duties include but are not limited to:
- Applies Federal Acquisition Regulations in preparing request for proposals (RFP) and request for quotes (RFQ) to ensure full compliance;
- Oversees planning, preparation and conduct of pre-solicitation, pre-proposal and/or post-awards functions on contracts;
- Prepares award contracts using contracting language, source selection procedures;
- Reviews contracts to ensure proper funding allocations and timely payments;
- Analysis acquisition processes, audits, and small business practices to ensure compliance;
- Assesses requests for the procurement of complex equipment and services;
- Provides technical advice, guidance and legal interpretation in all areas of contracting;
- Utilizes electronic contract management system(s);
- Communicates as a business advisor to internal and external acquisition customer; and
- Analysis acquisition processes, audits, and small business practices to ensure compliance.
Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. EST.
Compressed/Flexible: Available
Telework: Available - Ad Hoc telework (situational telework) as determined by the agency policy.
Virtual: This is not a virtual position.
Position Description Title/PD#: Contract Specialist~/ 00332A
Relocation/Recruitment Incentives: Not Authorized
Financial Disclosure Report: Required
Physical Requirements: The work is primarily sedentary, although there are regular and recurring construction inspections requiring a considerable amount of walking, stooping, bending and climbing.

conditions_of_employment:
- You must be able to pass a drug test.
